  "markdown": "Material family\n\n# Silk and textiles\n\nA cloth face with a sheen that changes as you move.\n\n![Close-up of Fromental hand-painted silk with dark marbled waves, Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-ig-09-800.webp)\n\nFromental hand-painted silk at Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square. Light picks out the marbled face; a physical sample in the room remains essential.Mr Wallcover project photograph, March 2019.[Four Seasons: the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\nBefore you choose\n\n**Consider it when**\n: You want a textile surface whose appearance changes with the light.\n\n**The trade-off**\n: Delicate faces can be less forgiving of marks and handling.\n\n**Before ordering**\n: See the sample in the room and confirm preparation and care requirements.\n\n01 · The finish\n\n## Joins\n\nSeams are planned so the light from the window does not catch a ridge.\n\n02 · The setting\n\n## Where it belongs\n\nRooms where light is part of the finish\n\n03 · Installation\n\n## Handling\n\nClean hands, the specified adhesive, and preparation written into the scope, including a lining where one is required.\n\n04 · Living with it\n\n## Care\n\nSilk marks quickly. Care is the maker’s note, usually dry. It is not a corridor vinyl.\n\nDigital colour is a guide. Order a cutting or a sample before you commit to a room. Some makers’ own sample routes are listed under [official buying routes](https://www.mrwallcover.com/buying-routes/). We can install material you have already bought, or source a family and install it. Either way, the next step is a short note about the room.\n\nBefore you order\n\n## For a high-value order\n\n- Workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months. [The aftercare page](https://www.mrwallcover.com/aftercare/) sets out what is covered.\n- Public liability, employers' liability and professional indemnity details are available on request.\n- Risk assessments and method statements (RAMS) on every job, with Dorin Burcus supervising on site.\n- A core team of six wallpaper hangers and six decorators who work together every day, scaling to 25–35 skilled tradespeople for large hotel programmes.\n- [For designers and architects](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/designers/)\n- [Download the specification schedule (CSV)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/downloads/wallcovering-specification-schedule.csv)\n- [Trade and contractors](https://www.mrwallcover.com/trade/)\n\nIllustrative material study · confirm the actual finish with a sample\n\nPause motion\n\nSave to shortlist\n\nSaved on this device only.\n\n[Discuss this material](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=source&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Asilk-and-textiles) [I already have it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Asilk-and-textiles)\n\n[How we install it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/silk-wallcovering-installation/)\n\nInstallation experience\n\n## On the record\n\nAt [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/), the hotel wallcoverings of 2019, about 5,000 m², included Fromental silks and Dedar. At [Raffles London at The OWO](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/raffles-london-the-owo/), selected suites have Vescom Alcantara.\n\nSilk shows the wall beneath it in side light, so preparation comes first; see [wall preparation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/wall-preparation/) and [silk wallcovering installation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/silk-wallcovering-installation/).\n\nPlan the detail\n\n## Useful reading\n\n- [Choosing wallcoverings](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/choosing-wallcoverings/)\n- [Wall preparation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/wall-preparation/)\n\nFrom our projects\n\n## Selected work\n\n- [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n- [Raffles London at The OWO, Whitehall](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/raffles-london-the-owo/)\n- [Brown's Hotel, Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\nMakers installed\n\n## Silk and textiles: makers we have hung\n\nEach in our own photograph of its product on the wall. Naming a maker records an installation, not an endorsement.\n\n- ![Collage of Fromental silk wallcovering details in a hotel room, Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-ig-01-800.webp)\n\n### Fromental\n\nInstalled at [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/).\n\n- ![Close-up of a lustrous Dedar wallcovering with horizontal sheen, Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-ig-06-800.webp)\n\n### Dedar\n\nInstalled at [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/).\n\nSilk and textiles: send a short note about the room, or tell us you already have the material.\n\n[Discuss this material](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=source&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Asilk-and-textiles) [I already have it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Asilk-and-textiles)\n\n[How we install silk and textiles](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/silk-wallcovering-installation/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last reviewed 9 October 2026\n",
